              </li>
          <li class="breadcrumb-item">
                  ESMA Signs Memorandum of Understanding With The Securities and Exchange Board of India
              </li>
        </ol>
  </nav>

  </div>

  </div>

        <div class="row no-gutters esma-news-page">
            <div class="order-1 order-lg-2 esma-news-page_content">
          <div class="region region-content">
    
<div class="container">
<article class="node node--type-news node--promoted node--view-mode-full">

  <h1>
    <a href="/press-news/esma-news/esma-signs-memorandum-understanding-securities-and-exchange-board-india" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">ESMA signs Memorandum of Understanding with the Securities and Exchange Board of India</span>
</a>
  </h1>
  <div class="sections">
      <div class="field field--name-field-news-section field--type-entity-reference field--label-hidden field__items">
              <div class="field__item">CCP</div>
              <div class="field__item">International cooperation</div>
          </div>
  </div>
  <div class="publication-date"> 04/09/2026</div>
  <div class="node__content">
    
            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-news-introduction field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p class="text-align-justify"><span>The European Securities and Markets Authority (ESMA), the EU’s financial markets regulator and supervisor, has signed a&nbsp;</span><a href="/sites/default/files/2026-09/MoU_ESMA-SEBI_CCPs.pdf"><span>Memorandum of Understanding (MoU)</span></a><span>&nbsp;with the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) to facilitate cooperation and exchange of information in relation to the recognition of central counterparties (CCPs) established in India and supervised by SEBI.</span></p>
</div>
      
            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-news-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p class="text-align-justify"><span>Following the signature of an MoU between ESMA and the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) earlier this year, this agreement marks a further significant step towards restoring access for EU clearing members to Indian CCPs and follows more than two years of sustained engagement between ESMA and Indian authorities.&nbsp;</span></p>
<p class="text-align-justify"><span>This MoU&nbsp;is the result of close and constructive cooperation between ESMA and SEBI and&nbsp;reflects ESMA’s strong commitment to international supervisory cooperation and mutual support to advance safe, resilient and open financial markets.</span></p>
<h4 class="text-align-justify"><span><strong>Next steps</strong></span></h4>
<p class="text-align-justify"><span>The MoU will allow CCPs established in India and supervised by SEBI to re-apply for recognition under EMIR. It is a key requirement under Article 25 of the&nbsp;European Market Infrastructure Regulation (EMIR) for the recognition of third-country CCPs by ESMA.</span></p>
<p class="text-align-justify"><span>ESMA is continuing discussions with the International Financial Services Centres Authority (IFSCA) with a view to concluding a similar cooperation arrangement.</span></p>
<p class="text-align-justify">&nbsp;</p>
<p><span>Further information:</span></p>
<h6><span lang="FR"><strong>Tayfun Yilmaz</strong></span></h6>
<p><span lang="FR">Communications Officer</span><br><a href="mailto:press@esma.europa.eu"><span lang="FR">press@esma.europa.eu</span></a><span lang="FR">&nbsp;</span></p>
</div>
      
  </div>

    
        <div class="container">
      <div class="teaser teaser--library-documents">
        <article class="node node--type-news node--promoted node--view-mode-full">
          <div class="teaser__content-title">
            <h5>
              Related Documents
            </h5>
            <div class="teaser__button--wrapper">
              <button class="download_all_files btn btn-link">Download All Files</button>
              <button class="download_selected_files btn btn-link">Download Selected Files</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="teaser__content">

            <table>
              <tr>
                <th>
